From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: Use the 8-bit PHY setting for YCbCr 4:2:2

The PHY tables give each TMDS rate a setting per colour depth, and
hdmi_phy_configure_dwc_hdmi_3d_tx() picks the depth from the output
bus format. YCbCr 4:2:2 is 12 bits a sample, but its container runs at
the 8-bit TMDS rate: the 12-bit setting multiplies a clock that needs
no multiplying. On the H616, 4:2:2 at 235.5 MHz showed no signal on a
monitor that takes it from an RK3528, and a picture with this change.

Use the 8-bit setting for 4:2:2.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff -urN a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -1613,6 +1613,10 @@ static int hdmi_phy_configure_dwc_hdmi_3d_tx(struct dw_hdmi *hdmi,
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/* 4:2:2's 12-bit container runs at the 8-bit TMDS rate */
+	if (hdmi_bus_fmt_is_yuv422(hdmi->hdmi_data.enc_out_bus_format))
+		depth = DW_HDMI_RES_8;
+
 	/* PLL/MPLL Cfg - always match on final entry */
 	for (; mpll_config->mpixelclock != ~0UL; mpll_config++)
 		if (mtmdsclock <= mpll_config->mpixelclock)
